                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Short version: Broken Expansion, Broken Achievements, Dead Multiplayer, Overpriced\n\nThe game only seems to work if you disable expansions and use the same very limited amount of buildings over and over, If you try to load a multiplayer game with more buildings enabled it spits out a connection error and from what I could gather this issue doesn't seem uncommon either. Without the expansions however the game loses a lot of replay value as there's just barely any variation.\n\nThe interface is fiddly at times and the auto-assignment of animals gets irritating very quickly since you have to wait until it's your turn again before you can fix the bad decisions the AI makes for you. \n\nAchievements don't work (with the exception of \"noob\" for trying out the game) which is a minor nitpick to people who don't care, but since I care I want to mention it anyway: They don't work. Maybe they work in ranked games but if so they are probably the worst achievement ideas ever (and given that most of them have really low completion rates, I assume I'm not alone in this either). Trying to get into 1000 ranked games is very idealistic, winning 1000.. well noone has ever done it before, so go figure. Let alone you can't set a time limit for people to react to your moves (it's either short or a whole day).  \n\nBut honestly you wouldn't want to play this game a 1000 times or more against people you don't know as there's just not enough variety. It's not chess where there is a lot of variety in terms of approaches. It's a casual fun boardgame intended for two friends or playing. Playing against someone you neither know nor communicate with takes away huge aspects of what makes boardgames like this charming. It just becomes a dull and dragged out exercise very quickly.\n\nThey are way better, less broken and more satisfying ways to waste 10 bucks.",
